---
description: Delegate implementation tasks to the configured local Qwen Code worker
alwaysApply: true
---

When the owner requests local-worker delegation, use Qwen Code backed by Ollama's `anzu-qwen-worker:latest`. This worker reads and edits the selected checkout and runs tests itself.

From the active checkout, invoke through your terminal:

```powershell
powershell.exe -NoProfile -File .\tools\qwen-worker\Invoke-QwenWorker.ps1 -Repo "<absolute path to the active checkout or worktree>" -Task "<specific implementation subtask and acceptance criteria>"
```

For long tasks use `-TaskFile "<absolute UTF-8 task file path>"` instead of `-Task`. Assign actual implementation, not only advice. Follow AGENTS.md and docs/PROCESS.md, name one ticket/subtask, preserve unrelated edits, and avoid editing the same files concurrently with the worker. Inspect its diff and reported test results before accepting the work.

The model and Qwen Code must already be installed and configured as described in tools/qwen-worker/README.md. Do not download or change models automatically. The endpoint is local-only with no paid fallback. Terminal delegation does not redirect Cursor's own model calls. Report missing terminal access or failed delegation plainly.
